# --- LLM · DeepSeek through the OpenAI-compatible API ----------------------
# WEBHOOK_API_KEY empty -> POST /webhook/alerts answers 503 webhook disabled; WEBHOOK_IP_ALLOWLIST empty -> deny all (DEC-040).
# LLM_MODEL_VERIFIER empty means "same model as the proposer" (§6.3).
# LLM_THINKING: disabled (the default since 06/09 — DEC-042) | enabled. Sent as extra_body.thinking.type and part of every measurement's cache key. P7's B4 ablation flips it; nothing else should.
# LLM_RESPONSE_FORMAT: json_object (the default) | json_schema (DEC-218). `json_schema` makes ①'s calls (proposer and verifier, first and repair) send the output schema for the provider to enforce, generated from output_schemas.json; one call the provider refuses with HTTP 400/422 is sent again as json_object and the run carries the warning response_format_fallback. ② and the RAG calls always send json_object.
# TRIAGE_RAG_FP_BELOW_PCT: an integer 0..100 (DEC-219), 0 (the default) = off. With N > 0, when an alert's RAG lookup kept a match and the best match (the "trùng X%" the alert page shows) is below N, ① answers false_positive whatever the model said; false_positive is then ①'s default answer: the run records it in gate_result.rag_rule and steps["3r"], keeps the model's own answer as proposed_verdict, and is not a gate force (forced false, no llm.gate_forced event). No lookup, a failed lookup, no match, entries dropped by the token budget or RAG off: the model's verdict stays. The trial sets 80; the containers must be recreated, not restarted.
# LLM_TIMEOUT_S: a wall-clock deadline per model call, enforced by the adapter — the SDK/httpx timeout it was mapped to bounds only the gap between received bytes (measured 05/09: 139.1 s completed under timeout=120; DEC-033).
# The model name is provisional; P1-T01 pins it by measurement.

